WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.301 line:92%
-Our first guest tonight i

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.102 line:92%
an Emmy Award-winning acto

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from hit shows
like "Cheers,"

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.672 size:84% position:42%
"Curb Your Enthusiasm,"
and "The Good Place."

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.606 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He stars in "Mr. Mayor,"

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.709
which airs Thursday nights
at 8:00 p.m. here on NBC.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Now, I know

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:15.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bunch of you independent
thinkers wouldn't -- [ Scoff ]

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:19.085
wouldn't even wear masks,
but what about helmets?

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's simple.
Download our free

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.491 line:92%
helmet-sharing app, Safe LA.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
Use the map feature
to locate a helmet.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:33.233
Now, you're ready to enter
the unique 14-digit code

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, uh, releases
the helmet security cover.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.571 line:92%
You then have 20 seconds to --

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.239 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Are you kidding me?

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.107 size:81% position:41%
Couldn't we just them
in a bin or something?

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] I don't know
-Okay. Alright.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.144 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.946 line:92%
one of the best, Ted Danson.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Ted?

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm great.
How are you?

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:53.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nice to see your face.
-It's nice to see
your face, too.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you in a sitcom kitchen,
right now,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.524 line:92%
or your personal kitchen?

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a new-build rental
up in Vancouver,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.596 size:78% position:39% line:92%
so it is very similar

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-to a sitcom kitchen.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right, now,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were in Vancouver,
I should say,

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your lovely bride,
Mary Steenburgen.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you guys seem to work ou
your schedule very well,

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:18.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you are not shooting
at the same time that often.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.147
-Yeah. You know, you would think
that it'd be more fun

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.784
to work at the same time
and then be able to go off

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:28.488
on this wonderful vacation
together, but, truth is,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:32.225
especially nowadays,
it's nice to have one of us home

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
to catch the other.
You know,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
cook and do housekeeping
and all that stuff,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I'm actually
really good at.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're good at housekeeping
in general?

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
I have no idea why.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.407 size:78% position:39% line:92%
My dad used to do it.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
I find it very satisfying
to make something dirty, clean

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So this is not --
By the way,

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.450 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you know my wife, Alexi.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.954
This is very much a qualit
she has that I don't have.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you're claiming
this is something

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.990 line:92%
that's always been true of you

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Yes.
Before I had a -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I could afford
a vacuum cleaner,

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:13.466
I would go around on my hand
and knees, picking up, you know,

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:17.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
lint and little pieces
of something from the carpet

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-This is really kind of sad.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.340 line:92%
Can we change the subject?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I'm just happy you finall
got that vacuum money.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, so, I'm also happy,
you know,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:33.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Good Place"
ended this wonderful run,

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.554 line:92%
tied a bow on a fantastic show

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think myself,
everybody in the industry,

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
was very worried
that you were not going

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.094
to land on your feet and, yet...
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:45.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
here you are, right away,
doing another sitcom.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
How quickly
after "The Good Place"

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.968 line:92%
were you aware of this project

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fact
that you would be doing it

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Actually,
before we finished shootin

00:02:53.840 --> 00:03:00.613
because Mike Schur, our creator,
knew, before the season started,

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:04.184
that this would be the las
season of "The Good Place.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:07.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he let us all know,
so we really had, you know

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
five or six months
of preparation,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
of being able to say goodbye
and also move on.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:18.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mike Schur, who I got to know
working with him at "SNL,"

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now, of course,
you're working with Tina Fey

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Robert Carlock,
who I knew the same way.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're all friends with Mike,
vice versa,

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.275
but "Mr. Mayor" is a very
different kind of show,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
don't you think?

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yes.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:36.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a lot sillier
and, boy, do we go fast.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:40.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I kind of grew u
in the "Cheers"

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Here's a joke.
Really funny, wasn't it?

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-Great. Let's have a laugh

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, we're going
to move on now," you know.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is like
you just tear through the joke

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.867 line:92%
and, you know, buckle up.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can always rewind it,
if you want, and check it out,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:04:02.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they don't stop
for the laugh, so.

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:06.679
Yeah, at 73, I'm having to learn
how to speak quickly.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's interesting
because, you know,

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.616 line:92%
the main difference, of course

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:12.852
is that, "Cheers,"
there was a live studio audience

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was reacting
to very funny jokes.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
As somebody
who watched "Cheers,"

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
I greatly appreciated watching
you all in the laughter,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, especially
on a show like "Cheers,"

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:25.164 size:84% position:42%
it must've been weird,
figuring out what to do

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.466 line:92%
while the audience was laughing.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.635 size:78% position:39%
I read -- and please
tell me this is true,

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.904
because it made me very happy --
that you also didn't know

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.607 size:88% position:44%
what to do, as an actor,
and they gave you a note

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:38.211 size:84% position:42%
on what to do while the
audience was laughing.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:41.147 size:78% position:39%
-Yes. It started out,
"Just eat a peanut.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just say your joke,
eat a peanut."

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, we found out
that wasn't funny,

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.654 size:88% position:44% line:92%
so we moved to pretzels.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ]
Ate a lot of pretzels.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.156 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know, it's funny,

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:53.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you do need,
with a live audience,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:58.931
you do need that, in case
your joke isn't that funny

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.066 line:92%
and you thought it might be,

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:04.370
you do need that thing to go to,
so you don't just go...

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know?
"Oh, no. It wasn't funny."

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's --
I mean, I was going to say

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
what an interesting thing,
I would love to experience it,

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:17.884
but you might know I used to
do this show with an audience.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:20.053
So I'm kind of finding out
in real time what it's lik

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:24.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go from a "Cheers"
to a Carlock/Fey project.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:26.659 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Ah, it's -- it's crazy.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:31.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now with COVID, they're --
before -- we started --

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
it took us a year
to shoot nine episodes

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of this
doggone pandemic.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
It started out
that they were on the floor,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
in Video Village watching,

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you could go around
the corner,

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you could see
that they were enjoying it

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
or it was funny or
it needed work or whatever

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
we had the nine-month hiatus

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.053 line:92%
because of COVID, the shutdown

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:58.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when we came back,
things were vastly different

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:03.796
They were in New York on a
computer screen Zooming with us,

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.466 line:92%
and we had masks and shields

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you'd come up --
You know, "Is that Tina?

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess so."
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:14.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"She's giving me a note,
and I'm don't -- like, okay.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:17.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it was not as much
fun, I'll have to admit.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing, though,
that Bobby spoke about

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:24.016
and I actually moderated a panel
with you and the cast,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:24.817 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and it seems to be true

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that because you had
this very long gap

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:30.189 size:84% position:42%
from shooting the pilot
to going back to work

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:30.857 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and then another gap

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:34.560
from when you started shooting
the first episodes until now

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
you did get very close
as a cast.

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That must be nice.

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was.
It was very nice.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the first three
episodes --

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know I was just,
"Can I do this?

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
What am I doing?
Learn your lines."

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we had
that nine months,

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:54.881
and it was, I mean, obviousl
so intensely scary, disturbing

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:58.151 line:92%
all those things, the shut-ins

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:01.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we started to Zoom
with each other

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
just for no reason
and catch up with each other

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:08.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you kind of really
learn some --

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, probably you had
a deeper cut

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:13.166 size:88% position:44%
at who these people were
if you hadn't done it.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
We went through
Black Lives Matters,

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:18.871 size:81% position:41%
and we went through so
many different phases

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:23.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this astounding, you know
time that we're living in

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
that by the time we came back,
we were much closer.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:28.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
I really love these people

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:30.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a --
It's a wonderful cast.

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:33.252 size:81% position:41%
Ted, one of the prices
of being as excellent

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.253 line:92%
for as long as you have been

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:37.356
is that it's impossible for yo
now to be a revelation, right?

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.725
Nobody is watching a show, being
like, "You know who is funny

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:42.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ted Danson."
You've established that.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:45.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Holly Hunter
is kind of a revelation.

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.466 line:92%
She's so wonderful in the show

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've seen her
be funny before,

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:49.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
but to see her be funny
on TV like this

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:50.870 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is just such a delight.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:56.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she's -- she's intens
in this wonderful way.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know how when you play
tennis with somebody

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:01.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if they're better than you
your game comes up?

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:07.119
Man, she hits the tennis bal
back so fast, it is incredible

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:10.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's ferocious
and relentless, and --

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:13.392
Yeah, I'm really tickled
to be able to work with he

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:18.064
because I love her and hav
loved her acting for so long

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:21.334
And then, speaking of -- I don't
know if it's a revelation.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:25.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've always known
that Bobby Moynihan

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
is -- is just
out-of-the-gate funny,

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
but oh, my God,
he's wonderful on our show

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really --
It makes me genuinely happ

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:35.848
knowing you both personall
and what nice people you are

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:39.151
It makes me genuinely happ
to see you guys working together

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.454 line:92%
because you're great together.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:41.888 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:08:41.888 --> 00:08:46.592 size:88% position:44%
He is just the sweetest,
kindest, happiest daddy.

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.628 line:92%
You know, he's incredible.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:52.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I should note you are playing
the mayor of Los Angeles.

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:54.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a fictional mayor.
It's not based on anybody.

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:57.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it does seem nice to,
in this day and age,

00:08:57.737 --> 00:09:00.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
show people that anyone
can be an elected official

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:04.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that really strikes me
as what your character is.

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:11.050
-Yeah. No, I am that 73-year-old
very white, very rich guy

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:12.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
who should not
be still in the game.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:16.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
He should be irrelevant
and somehow lucks into it.

00:09:16.656 --> 00:09:21.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's this great lin
that's actually true

00:09:21.794 --> 00:09:25.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
where my staff is saying,
"Don't tell him,

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:31.203 size:84% position:42%
but the truth is that
he got 67% of the vote,

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:34.640 line:92%
but only 18% of Los Angele

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:40.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
votes in the mayoral elections
on an off year,

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:42.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
if it's not a presidential
election."

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:46.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I -- You know,
I got 8%, maybe, of the vote

00:09:46.886 --> 00:09:52.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
So -- And that's true.
That's literally what happens.

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:53.659 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Well, you're both --

00:09:53.659 --> 00:09:56.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
your character's both
incredibly underqualified,

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:58.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I still think
you're better than most.

00:09:58.397 --> 00:10:01.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is always just
such a delight to see you, Ted

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:02.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for making time
for us today.

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:05.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks for talking
about the show.

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:06.606 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Much love to everybody.

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:11.444
-And Mary did ask me to tell you
it's time to start cleaning up

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:12.878 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:16.849
"Mr. Mayor" airs Thursday nights
at 8:00 right here on NBC.

